  "body": "The spec isn't clear about what error `BluetoothRemoteGATTCharacteristic.startNotifications()` should return if the origin's permission to access the device is revoked (or if permission was lost while the operation is in flight).\n\nThe [`startNotifications()` algorithm](https://webbluetoothcg.github.io/web-bluetooth/#dom-bluetoothremotegattcharacteristic-startnotifications) says to reject with `SecurityError` when the characteristic is blocklisted:\n\n> 3. If this.uuid is blocklisted for reads, return a promise rejected with a \"SecurityError\" DOMException.\n\nHowever, the steps do not specify what should happen if permission to access the device has been revoked. I think it's reasonable to lump loss-of-permissions into the blocklist case.\n\nCould the spec clarify which `DOMException` should be returned when permission is revoked?",
